# The variables Redline reads. Names only — never put a value in this file.
#
# Locally: copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill it in, or let
# scripts/setup-supabase.sh write the Supabase pair for you.
# On Vercel: Project → Settings → Environment Variables, same names. Redeploy
# after changing a NEXT_PUBLIC_ value; those are baked in at build time.

# ── The model, called through OpenRouter. Server only. ──────────────────────
# Without these the analysis and the question box fail with an error naming
# the missing variable. The model id is deliberately not written here; use the
# default model named in CLAUDE.md.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_MODEL=

# ── The account, which only keeps a reader's red lines. ─────────────────────
# Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API. The public key is labelled
# "anon public" on older projects and "publishable" on newer ones; either
# works. Never the service_role / secret key: this one ships to the browser.
# Leave both blank and the product still works, with sign-in hidden.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
